  "raw_text": "The session focused on building a terminal session capture script that uses the Unix `script` command to record Claude Code sessions and gzip them for long-term storage. The central question was whether compression to roughly 10% of original size was realistic. The model confirmed that 5-15x compression is achievable precisely because terminal output from Claude Code contains dense repetitive sequences \u2014 escape codes, line-drawing characters, and whitespace \u2014 which are exactly the patterns gzip exploits most effectively.",
